hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18047","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us, he said: My father informed me from Ziyad ibn Mina from Abu Said ibn Abi Fadalah al-Ansari, and he was among the Companions, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah gathers the first and the last for a Day in which there is no doubt, a caller shall call: Whoever associated in a deed he did for Allah Almighty anyone, let him seek its reward from other than Allah, for Allah is the most free of partners from partnership."
